{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.EHartreeTraceRatio","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.EHartreeTraceRatio","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.TorusKnotGenusFourUnique"],"declarations":19,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.EHartreeTraceRatio.unique_self_conjugate_partition_of_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.EHartreeTraceRatio.unique_self_conjugate_partition_of_four","kind":"theorem","line":244,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EHartreeTraceRatio.lean#L244-L249","doc":"`(2,2)` is the **unique** self-conjugate partition of `4` (the fact the\ncorpus cites for the EM block — `(2,2)ᵀ = (2,2)`, while `(4)↔(1,1,1,1)` and\n`(3,1)↔(2,1,1)` swap), re-derived here by `decide`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.EHartreeTraceRatio.em_channel_forced_to_two_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.EHartreeTraceRatio.em_channel_forced_to_two_two","kind":"theorem","line":220,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EHartreeTraceRatio.lean#L220-L242","doc":"**Round 25 (the EM channel is forced to `(2,2)`).**\n\nThe 2-strand EM coupling is the sign rep of `S₂` (the singlet `e₋ = Λ²A`,\n`prop:em-coupling-projection`); a covalent bond is two such singlets (Pauli-2),\nso the pair sits in `sgn ⊠ sgn` on `S₂ × S₂`.  Inducing to the 4-strand\nmolecular braid gives — witnessed (multiplicity 1 each, Frobenius reciprocity) in\n`e-hartree-round25-em-channel-induction.witness.json` —\n\n`Ind_{S₂×S₂}^{S₄}(sgn ⊠ sgn) = (2,2) ⊕ (2,1,1) ⊕ (1,1,1,1)`.\n\nA parity-symmetric covalent bound state is closed under the Hopf antipode\n`S : V_λ ↦ V_{λᵀ}`, so its channel must be **self-transpose**.  Among the three\ninduced summands `(2,2)` is the unique self-conjugate one (proved here), so the\nEM bound-state channel is **forced** to `(2,2)`; `(2,1,1)` is the force-carrier\nchannel and `(1,1,1,1)` the decoupled channel.\n\nThis *grounds* the `(2,2)=EM` identification in the covalent-pair structure; it\ndoes **not** close the conjecture — the `sgn ⊠ sgn` physical input and the\nround-20 `α²` algebra remain (and `prop:force-carrier-intertwining-correspondence`\nis e-hartree-conditional, so the `(2,1,1)` coincidence is corroboration only). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.EHartreeTraceRatio.conjPart","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.EHartreeTraceRatio.conjPart","kind":"def","line":214,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EHartreeTraceRatio.lean#L214-L218","doc":"Conjugate (transpose) of a partition `λ` given as a weakly-decreasing list:\n`λᵀ_i = #{ parts ≥ i }`.  Computable, so the channel-selection facts below close\nby `decide`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.EHartreeTraceRatio.forceCarrier_complexity_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.EHartreeTraceRatio.forceCarrier_complexity_unique","kind":"theorem","line":188,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EHartreeTraceRatio.lean#L188-L212","doc":"**Round 24, LEG 1 (the force-carrier complexity is context-free).**\n\nThe categorical force-carrier complexity `cplx = q·[9]_q·[10]_q` (`= 1/α_EM`,\n[`prop:em-coupling-projection`]) is the **same** for any two distinct genus-4\ncoprime torus knots — it depends only on the forced crossing-number multiset\n`{9, 10}`, not on any molecular context.  Hence the round-23 normaliser\n`(q·[9]_q·[10]_q)²` is **not** a free, \"molecular\" choice: there is no\nmolecular-vs-free version of the complexity to reuse, because the force-carrier\nsector is unique (Bring uniqueness).  This formally discharges LEG 1 of the\nmolecular-reuse assumption.\n\nLEG 2 — that the dressed `(2,2)` block *is* the EM exchange (so it costs this\n`cplx`), and that the covalent pair contributes `cplx²` — is the conjecture's\nown `(2,2)=EM` identification plus the covalent Pauli-2 count; it is **not**\nformalised here as discharged (and cannot be, without circularity, since\n`prop:force-carrier-intertwining-correspondence` is itself conditional on\n`conj:e-hartree`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.EHartreeTraceRatio.forceCarrier_crossings_forced","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.EHartreeTraceRatio.forceCarrier_crossings_forced","kind":"theorem","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EHartreeTraceRatio.lean#L168-L186","doc":"**Round 24, LEG 1 (force-carrier crossing numbers are forced).**\n\nTwo *distinct* genus-4 coprime torus knots have crossing numbers `9` and `10`\n(in some order).  Reuses the proven genus-4 uniqueness\n(`QOU.Archimedean.torus_knot_genus_four_unique`): the only such knots are\n`T_{2,9}` (crossing `9`) and `T_{3,5}` (crossing `10`), and the distinctness\nhypothesis rules out the same-knot cases.  This is the structural fact behind\nthe round-23 \"molecular-reuse\" discharge: the force-carrier sector is unique. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.EHartreeTraceRatio.traceRatio_of_dressedChar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.EHartreeTraceRatio.traceRatio_of_dressedChar","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EHartreeTraceRatio.lean#L160-L166","doc":"Under a dressed-scalar-character context, the round-20 trace-ratio is the\n`C(q)·α²` form — combining the granted (witnessed) character with the proven\nalgebraic factorisation.  `cplx = q·[9]_q·[10]_q`, `α = 1/cplx`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.EHartreeTraceRatio.DressedScalarCharacter.chi_dressed_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.EHartreeTraceRatio.DressedScalarCharacter.chi_dressed_eq","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EHartreeTraceRatio.lean#L158-L158","doc":"its closed form `h·(q²+q⁻²)²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.EHartreeTraceRatio.DressedScalarCharacter.chi_dressed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.EHartreeTraceRatio.DressedScalarCharacter.chi_dressed","kind":"def","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EHartreeTraceRatio.lean#L156-L156","doc":"the K-shell-dressed character on the `(2,2)` block. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.EHartreeTraceRatio.DressedScalarCharacter.chi_bare_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.EHartreeTraceRatio.DressedScalarCharacter.chi_bare_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EHartreeTraceRatio.lean#L154-L154","doc":"it vanishes (hook-support; `(2,2)` is the unique non-hook). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.EHartreeTraceRatio.DressedScalarCharacter.chi_bare","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.EHartreeTraceRatio.DressedScalarCharacter.chi_bare","kind":"def","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EHartreeTraceRatio.lean#L152-L152","doc":"the bare Coxeter-word character on the `(2,2)` block. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.EHartreeTraceRatio.DressedScalarCharacter.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.EHartreeTraceRatio.DressedScalarCharacter.mk","kind":"ctor","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EHartreeTraceRatio.lean#L150-L150","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.EHartreeTraceRatio.DressedScalarCharacter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.EHartreeTraceRatio.DressedScalarCharacter","kind":"structure","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EHartreeTraceRatio.lean#L137-L158","doc":"**Round-19 dressed scalar-block character — abstract context (§3b-cond).**\n\nThe repo convention records a concrete seminormal (Hoefsmit) character as\n*data verified numerically*, rather than re-proving it from representation\nmatrices — see `QOU.BraidKnot.QHeckeSeminormalCharacterClosure`.  Here the\nround-19 values are witnessed in\n`e-hartree-round19-dressed-scalar-block.witness.json` (cross-checked to\n`9·10⁻¹⁶` against the seminormal builder `hecke_characters.py`):\n\n* `chi_bare = χ_(2,2)(σ₁σ₂σ₃) = 0` — the bare hook-support vanishing (`(2,2)`\n  is the unique non-hook of `4`; q-Murnaghan–Nakayama, Ram 1991);\n* `chi_dressed = χ_(2,2)(σ₁σ₂^{(5)}σ₃) = h·(q²+q⁻²)²` — the K-shell `m = 5`\n  dressed value (`= h·(dim_q V_(2,2))²`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.EHartreeTraceRatio.hartree_token_from_trace_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.EHartreeTraceRatio.hartree_token_from_trace_ratio","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EHartreeTraceRatio.lean#L119-L135","doc":"**Round-20 ↔ Hartree-class wiring (conditional on the q-dimension bridge).**\n\nThe `EHartreeCategoricalDerivation` class (sibling block\n`conj:e-hartree-categorical-derivation`) posits\n`E_h = c₂ · m_e · c_q² · α²`.  Round 20 identifies the candidate\ncoefficient `c₂ = C(q) = h·(q²+q⁻²)²` (the dressed `(2,2)` trace-ratio\ncoefficient).  The identification `c₂ = C(q)` is **the open q-dimension-layer\nbridge** — Mechanism B (the LP-dual-smoothness route) was *refuted* in round 21\n(the separated-atom point is a kink, not a smooth facet), so this hypothesis is\nexplicitly carried, not derived.  Under it, the Hartree token takes the\nround-20 form.  Pure rewriting; the content is the named hypothesis `hc2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.EHartreeTraceRatio.trace_ratio_eq_C_mul_alpha_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.EHartreeTraceRatio.trace_ratio_eq_C_mul_alpha_sq","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EHartreeTraceRatio.lean#L105-L117","doc":"**Round-20 trace-ratio, assembled.**\n\nGiven the round-19 dressed character `chi22 = h·(q²+q⁻²)²` and the complexity\n`cplx = q·[9]_q·[10]_q`, the trace-ratio equals `C(q)·α²` with the *derived*\n`O(1)` coefficient `C(q) = h·(q²+q⁻²)²` and `α = 1/cplx`.  Sorry-free; the\ncontent is `trace_ratio_factorisation` with `C(q)` named. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.EHartreeTraceRatio.trace_ratio_factorisation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.EHartreeTraceRatio.trace_ratio_factorisation","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EHartreeTraceRatio.lean#L95-L103","doc":"**Trace-ratio factorisation (round 20).**\n\nThe molecular scalar-block trace-ratio `χ₂₂ / cplx²` equals `χ₂₂ · (1/cplx)²`\nwhere the EM coupling is `α = 1/cplx`, `cplx = q·[9]_q·[10]_q`.  Pure algebra —\nthe step that exhibits the `α_EM²` scaling once the dressed character `χ₂₂` and\nthe complexity normaliser are in hand. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.EHartreeTraceRatio.qbracket_four_div_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.EHartreeTraceRatio.qbracket_four_div_two","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EHartreeTraceRatio.lean#L79-L93","doc":"**The bracket reduction `[4]_q / [2]_q = q² + q⁻²`.**\n\nThis is `dim_q V_(2,2)`, the q-dimension of the scalar Wedderburn block that\nactivates under K-shell dressing (round 19); it is the `C(q)`-defining factor\nin the round-20 trace-ratio.  Holds for `0 < q`, `q ≠ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.EHartreeTraceRatio.qsq_sub_inv_sq_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.EHartreeTraceRatio.qsq_sub_inv_sq_ne","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EHartreeTraceRatio.lean#L66-L77","doc":"For `0 < q` and `q ≠ 1`, `q² − (q⁻¹)² ≠ 0` (the `[2]`-amplitude squared). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.EHartreeTraceRatio.qsub_inv_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.EHartreeTraceRatio.qsub_inv_ne","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EHartreeTraceRatio.lean#L52-L64","doc":"For `0 < q` and `q ≠ 1`, the amplitude `q − q⁻¹` is nonzero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.EHartreeTraceRatio.qbracket","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.EHartreeTraceRatio.qbracket","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EHartreeTraceRatio.lean#L48-L50","doc":"Balanced q-integer `[n]_q = (qⁿ − (q⁻¹)ⁿ)/(q − q⁻¹)` over `ℝ`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}